ak9x|n|The act of winding or turning; a turn; a bend; a twist; a winding. ; Air naturally in motion with any degree of velocity; a current of air. ; Air artificially put in motion by any force or action; as, the wind of a cannon ball; the wind of a bellows. ; Breath modulated by the respiratory and vocal organs, or by an instrument. ; Power of respiration; breath. ; Air or gas generated in the stomach or bowels; flatulence; as, to be troubled with wind. ; Air impregnated with an odor or scent. ; A direction from which the wind may blow; a point of the compass; especially, one of the cardinal points, which are often called the four winds. ; A disease of sheep, in which the intestines are distended with air, or rather affected with a violent inflammation. It occurs immediately after shearing. ; Mere breath or talk; empty effort; idle words. ; The dotterel.	a:3mtf,119,57;3wub,109,51;4xj2,105,6;7b18,98,8;2qgc,92,19;aiil,91,13;3wu6,90,6;6evj,89,16;8tvx,89,3679;8w0m,89,11;106f,86,2;23dx,82,5;oz8,81,3;5fvz,79,6;1zoj,79,38~8tvx,89,3679;7vmg,50,1217;95fj,52,1048;43ai,33,788;8egs,2,265;8s1h,11,240;1n86,43,189;abfv,35,186;p0f,25,185;5en8,16,170;5n0z,19,168;45jk,34,154;gbw,45,138;92g4,72,137;5cam,4,134	v:7dr6,85,164;46ak,85,29;ag9c,81,51;8xxf,79,5;7mr4,77,4;9b61,70,76;81s1,70,4;9mkz,69,8;87j3,69,3;3wu6,64,1;4mfz,61,4;3mtf,60,1;aj8a,60,7;yxz,55,4;5hdh,55,1~7dr6,85,164;7toc,14,84;9b61,70,76;1br7,32,67;ag9c,81,51;zvx,45,41;8pgi,21,35;46ak,85,29;7ywe,40,28;6shx,22,22;p0n,45,18;al71,41,16;876h,52,15;6si3,50,14;9tna,29,12	V:zvp,138,66;zw6,92,864;zvk,89,6;46ae,89,5;aj8n,86,7;78s0,85,10;2i9w,85,18;8792,84,2;aj81,83,3;4rmr,82,1;zvx,80,470;zbg,80,190;3wua,78,15;aj8u,74,19;7qbe,73,5~zw6,92,864;zvx,80,470;zbg,80,190;1olc,12,172;84of,65,155;18lm,15,134;1ons,18,130;3d1w,45,97;8x1o,7,96;50s1,67,89;1amt,46,83;1bsr,15,73;443f,28,71;5zu0,7,68;7k5r,31,67	n:2e9z,109,6;5gbj,102,9;106f,96,4;6ngg,94,27;ah4i,90,6;tvo,87,8;6kyf,86,77;a5lf,85,9;s0y,85,5;5y7k,83,18;87j3,81,7;oz8,81,3;7dr6,76,87;6gw,72,39